EvalSuite[skillName=market-technical-analysis, evals=[Eval[id=1, prompt=Generate a technical analysis report for Apple (AAPL) as of 2023-10-27. The primary data provider (Provider A) is currently returning a 429 Too Many Requests error. The fallback provider (Provider B) has valid OHLCV data for that date. Ensure the report reflects the correct closing price and RSI(14) value from the available source., expectedOutput=The agent must detect the throttling of Provider A, automatically switch to Provider B, retrieve the verified data for 2023-10-27, and produce a report citing Provider B as the source. It must not fabricate data or fail due to the primary source error., files=[], expectations=[Must explicitly mention that Provider A was throttled/unavailable and that Provider B was used as the fallback., Must include the exact closing price and RSI(14) value retrieved from Provider B for 2023-10-27., Must not include any estimated or interpolated values for the missing data points., Must confirm the data timestamp corresponds exactly to 2023-10-27 (point-in-time integrity).]], Eval[id=2, prompt=Analyze the technical setup for Tesla (TSLA) on 2024-01-15. Both the primary and secondary data providers return empty responses for this specific date due to a market holiday or data gap. Do not estimate the price., expectedOutput=The agent must report that data is 'unavailable' for TSLA on 2024-01-15 after exhausting all configured sources. It must not generate a report with estimated prices or indicators., files=[], expectations=[Must explicitly state that data is 'unavailable' for the requested date., Must not contain any numerical price values (Open, High, Low, Close) or indicator values for TSLA on 2024-01-15., Must not attempt to interpolate or estimate values from adjacent trading days., Must list the providers that were queried and failed.]], Eval[id=3, prompt=Create a technical report for Microsoft (MSFT) as of 2023-11-01. The verified snapshot shows a closing price of $370.50. However, the momentum indicator module returns an RSI(14) of 85, which contradicts the neutral trend suggested by the moving averages. Flag this discrepancy rather than smoothing it over., expectedOutput=The agent must produce a report that accurately cites the closing price of $370.50 and the RSI of 85. It must explicitly flag the discrepancy between the high momentum reading and the neutral trend indicators, rather than inventing a reconciled narrative or ignoring the outlier., files=[], expectations=[Must cite the exact closing price of $370.50 from the verified snapshot., Must cite the exact RSI(14) value of 85., Must include a specific warning or flag section noting the discrepancy between the high RSI and neutral trend indicators., Must not alter the RSI value to fit a 'neutral' narrative.]], Eval[id=4, prompt=Retrieve technical indicators for Amazon (AMZN) for the analysis date of 2023-09-20. The user requests data for 2023-09-21, but the system clock is set to 2023-09-20. Ensure point-in-time integrity is enforced., expectedOutput=The agent must clamp the data request to the analysis date of 2023-09-20, ignoring the user's request for 2023-09-21 if it is in the future relative to the system clock/analysis date. The report must reflect data available up to 2023-09-20., files=[], expectations=[Must explicitly state that the analysis date is clamped to 2023-09-20., Must not include any data points dated 2023-09-21., Must retrieve and report OHLCV and indicators for 2023-09-20., Must mention that future data requests were restricted to maintain point-in-time integrity.]]]]
